From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO for Linux

CromIKO as an app of its own on Linux, like CromIKO-Windows.patch on
Windows, so that it runs next to Chromium and Cromite:

- Its own profile folder, ~/.config/cromiko (and ~/.cache/cromiko),
  instead of the one of Chromium.
- Its desktop entry is cromiko.desktop, which pack_linux.py puts in the
  .tar.xz and install.sh adds to the apps of the desktop. It also names
  the class of the windows ("cromiko"), so desktops show them with the
  entry and its icon, and the default browser setting names CromIKO.
- The icons of the windows and of the desktop entry, and the small logo of
  the browser UI on Linux: the white mascot on the charcoal tile, like the
  Android and Windows app icons (tools/cromiko/gen_linux_icons.py).

License: GPL-3.0-only - https://spdx.org/licenses/GPL-3.0-only.html
